resistor-circuit-consumer-power-choices-3 = It stays the same
resistor-circuit-build-question-2 = The circuit has a source, a key, a resistor (the consumer), an ammeter and a voltmeter. We set the source to { $volts }, write down the instruments each time and find the power P = U · I. How many times does the power grow if the voltage across the resistor is doubled?
